        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is SereneLife a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is a legitimate budget brand, owned by Sound Around, Inc. of Brooklyn, the company behind Pyle. Its treadmills are fine for walking and light jogging, but every model has a belt of about 39 to 40 inches, a top speed of 8 mph or less and a one-year warranty on Amazon, so they are not running treadmills.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes SereneLife treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              SereneLife says it is part of the Sound Around, Inc. family of brands, headquartered in Brooklyn, New York. Its support line is (888) 318-7953 and its support email is a pyleusa.com address, shared with Pyle.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty comes with a SereneLife treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The Amazon listings give one year. SereneLife’s site advertises a three-year limited warranty for qualifying products registered within 30 days, but excludes some product types and does not list which treadmills qualify. Register anyway and ask SereneLife to confirm your term in writing.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much weight can a SereneLife treadmill hold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Most SereneLife listings give 265 lb, and one gives 264 lb. The SLFTRD20 says 220 lb on Amazon and 265 lb on SereneLife’s own site, so use 220 lb for that model. None states more than 265 lb.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How fast does a SereneLife treadmill go?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Between 5 and 8 mph, depending on the model. The SLFTRD26BT and SLFTRD20 go to 6 mph, the SLFTRDHB27 to 7.5 mph by its bullets, and a 2.0 HP portable model to 8 mph. The SLFTRD14.5 walking pad goes to 5 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you run on a SereneLife treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Only a slow jog. Every SereneLife belt is about 39 to 40 inches long, much shorter than the 55 to 60 inches usually recommended for running, and the fastest model tops out at 8 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

